    {
      "id": "hp.natural_durability_pct",
      "title": "Natural Durability: percent of the HP that comes from STA, by rank",
      "value": {"1": 2, "2": 5, "3": 10, "4": 12},
      "unit": "percent (cumulative)",
      "seal": "player",
      "source": [
        {"kind": "client-file", "ref": "dbstr_us.txt"},
        {"kind": "public-text", "ref": "eqlwiki AA data, revision 151303, as extracted by eqlbuilds.com"}
      ],
      "date": "2026-10-25",
      "status": "active",
      "notes": "AA 107, type 4 in the client's text: increases your maximum base health (derived from your stamina) by #1%. The ranks (2, 5, 10 and 12 percent, costs 2, 4, 6 and 2) are the wiki's data. It scales only the HP that comes from STA (the hp_fac x STA' of 5 + base_hp + hp_fac x STA'), not the constant, the class base or the flat HP of items and buffs. The model assumes the top rank for every class, as it assumes Combat Stability 3 of 3; the window floors the STA part first and the scaled part after."
    },
