    {
      "id": "haste.unbound_alacrity",
      "title": "Unbound Alacrity: effect on haste",
      "value": "adds 10 haste and raises the cap by 10",
      "unit": "text",
      "seal": "developer",
      "source": [
        {"kind": "public-text", "ref": "patch notes 2026-07-28, Unbound Alacrity (\"increase in your current and maximum haste value\")"},
        {"kind": "url", "ref": "https://eqlwiki.com/Haste_Guide"}
      ],
      "date": "2026-10-22",
      "status": "active",
      "notes": "A trio with a Monk gets 10 haste that stacks with the best spell haste and the best worn haste, up to haste.cap_pct_with_monk (the cap already includes its 10). The wiki's Haste Guide says it grants up to 10% haste and raises the cap by 10%; the patch notes say it raises both the current and the maximum haste value. 2026-10-22: the weapon index is paid the haste the kit counts (the spell haste of the buffs it takes, this 10 included, plus the best worn haste it wears, up to the cap), not a haste the scenario could reach; the solver chooses the buffs and the haste item together with the weapons."
    },
